IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-16: Article 16 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): obligations of providers of high-risk AI systems.
-- Section 3 of Chapter III, lines 374-390 of the consolidated text. Unchanged by the Omnibus (no `▼M1` passage in these lines).
-- Layer 1, the law objectively. Each point (a) to (l) is one decision function (has the provider met it?) and one regulative rule (the provider MUST).
-- The party is "Providers of high-risk AI systems": a person who holds that role (Art 3(3), or deemed one under Art 25) asks these functions; the role is not re-asked here.
-- How to read a result (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (P3)"):
--   JUST TRUE   the facts show the duty met.
--   JUST FALSE  the duty applies and the facts show it not met: the flat "shall" of the chapeau (fork F-bare-shall in NOTES.md).
--   NOTHING     not covered: Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not yet apply to this system (Art 113(c), Art 111(2)), or the point limits itself
--               ("when under their control", "upon a reasoned request"), or Article 2(13) may limit the obligation (points outside the text).
--   A system cut off by Art 2(2) answers JUST FALSE (a flat "only ... shall apply").
-- Seams: S6 (Articles 43, 47, 48, 49: asked as plain BOOLEAN inputs, named for the Article they come from), S8 (Section 2), S1 (the route, inside the `AI system` record).

§ `Article 16: the twelve acts the provider shall do`

DECLARE `Art 16 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 16(a) ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2`
    `Art 16(b) indicate the name, registered trade name or registered trade mark and the contact address`
    `Art 16(c) have a quality management system in place which complies with Article 17`
    `Art 16(d) keep the documentation referred to in Article 18`
    `Art 16(e) keep the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system as referred to in Article 19`
    `Art 16(f) ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure referred to in Article 43`
    `Art 16(g) draw up an EU declaration of conformity in accordance with Article 47`
    `Art 16(h) affix the CE marking in accordance with Article 48`
    `Art 16(i) comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)`
    `Art 16(j) take the necessary corrective actions and provide information as required in Article 20`
    `Art 16(k) demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
    `Art 16(l) ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements`

§ `Article 16(a): compliance with the requirements of Section 2 (seam S8)`

-- src:378 | Providers of high-risk AI systems shall:
-- src:379 | (a) ensure that their high-risk AI systems are compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2;
@ref Art 16(a) (src:378-379)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(a) the provider has ensured that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall: (a) ensure that their high-risk AI systems are compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

@ref Art 16(a) (src:378-379)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 16 act`
`Art 16(a) the provider's duty to ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 16(a) ensure that the high-risk AI system is compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the high-risk AI system was not ensured to be compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)


§ `Article 16(b): the provider's name and contact address on the system, its packaging or its documentation`

-- "or, where that is not possible, on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, as applicable": the second place counts only where the first is not possible.
-- The particulars are "their name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, the address at which they can be contacted".
-- src:380 | (b) indicate on the high-risk AI system or, where that is not possible, on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, as applicable, their name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, the address at which they can be contacted;
@ref Art 16(b) (src:380)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the particulars are indicated on the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is not possible to indicate the particulars on the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars are indicated on its packaging or its accompanying documentation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(b) the provider has indicated its name, registered trade name or registered trade mark and its contact address` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the particulars are indicated on the high-risk AI system` OR (`it is not possible to indicate the particulars on the high-risk AI system` AND `the particulars are indicated on its packaging or its accompanying documentation`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) indicate on the high-risk AI system or, where that is not possible, on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, as applicable, their name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, the address at which they can be contacted"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

@ref Art 16(b) (src:380)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 16 act`
`Art 16(b) the provider's duty to indicate its name, registered trade name or registered trade mark and its contact address` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 16(b) indicate the name, registered trade name or registered trade mark and the contact address`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the name and contact address were not indicated"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)


