§ `Article 16(e): the automatically generated logs, "when under their control"`

-- "when under their control" limits the duty in its own wording: where the logs are not under the provider's control the point does not speak
-- (NOTHING, limited by its own wording); fork F-when-upon in NOTES.md.
-- src:383 | (e) when under their control, keep the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems as referred to in Article 19;
@ref Art 16(e) (src:383)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider keeps the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system as referred to in Article 19` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(e) the provider keeps the logs automatically generated by its high-risk AI system when under its control` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) when under their control, keep the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems" (the logs are not under its control)
        ELSE
             IF `the provider keeps the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system as referred to in Article 19`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) when under their control, keep the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems as referred to in Article 19" (the logs are under its control and are not kept)
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

@ref Art 16(e) (src:383)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 16 act`
`Art 16(e) the provider's duty to keep the logs automatically generated by its high-risk AI system` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system are under the provider's control`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 16(e) keep the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system as referred to in Article 19`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system were not kept"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the logs are not under the provider's control
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)


§ `Article 16(f): conformity assessment "prior to its being placed on the market or put into service" (seam S6: Article 43)`

-- The decision function asks whether the procedure of Article 43 has been completed; the time limit "prior to its being placed on the market or put into service"
-- is carried by the regulative rule (its deadline is the placement date in the `AI system` record). The clock of the rule is in days from the date asked (day 0).
-- A date asked that is already past the placement date leaves no time (deadline 0). The deadline is inclusive: an act on the placement day is counted as timely (fork F-prior-to in NOTES.md).
-- src:384 | (f) ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure as referred to in Article 43, prior to its being placed on the market or put into service;
@ref Art 16(f) (src:384)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the conformity assessment procedure of Article 43 has been completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(f) the provider has ensured that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the conformity assessment procedure of Article 43 has been completed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure as referred to in Article 43, prior to its being placed on the market or put into service"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

@ref Art 16(f) (src:384)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 16 act`
`Art 16(f) the provider's duty to ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 16(f) ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure referred to in Article 43`
         WITHIN daysLeft
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the conformity assessment procedure was not carried out before the high-risk AI system was placed on the market or put into service"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)
        placed MEANS `the AI system`'s `date placed on the market or put into service`
        daysLeft MEANS IF (Day placed) AT LEAST (Day `the date asked`) THEN (Day placed) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) ELSE 0


