§ `Article 16(k): demonstrating conformity "upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority"`

-- "upon a reasoned request": the duty is limited in its own wording; with no such request the point does not speak
-- (NOTHING, limited by its own wording); fork F-when-upon in NOTES.md.
-- src:389 | (k) upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority, demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2;
@ref Art 16(k) (src:389)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a national competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider has demonstrated the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(k) the provider has demonstrated the conformity of the high-risk AI system upon a reasoned request` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `a national competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(k) upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority, demonstrate the conformity" (no reasoned request has been made)
        ELSE
             IF `the provider has demonstrated the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(k) upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority, demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2" (a request was made and the conformity was not demonstrated)
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

@ref Art 16(k) (src:389)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `a national competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 16 act`
`Art 16(k) the provider's duty to demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system upon a reasoned request` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `a national competent authority has made a reasoned request to the provider`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 16(k) demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2 was not demonstrated"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or no reasoned request has been made
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)


§ `Article 16(l): accessibility requirements (Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882, borrowed)`

-- src:390 | (l) ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements in accordance with Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882.
@ref Art 16(l) (src:390)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements in accordance with Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 16(l) the provider has ensured that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements in accordance with Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(l) ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements in accordance with Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

@ref Art 16(l) (src:390)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 16 act`
`Art 16(l) the provider's duty to ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 16(l) ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the high-risk AI system was not ensured to comply with accessibility requirements"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 16, "", 0)

